  "map_id": "map:argonne-national-laboratory",
  "method": "DERIVED circle: radius from the sourced circumference, centre from the hall's outlines, relation from the design report; not traced from any map. (1) Radius: the APS operations page gives 'Circumference C 1103.609 m' for the 40-sector ring (src:geo-argonne-aps-sr-parameters), so R = C / 2 pi = 175.645 m; the older OSTI parameter list says 1104 m (src:geo-argonne-aps-parameters). The ring is 40 identical sectors of 9 degrees, so a circle of the same circumference departs from the orbit by less than the sagitta of one sector chord, R (1 - cos 4.5 deg) = 0.54 m. (2) Centre: OSM relation 3126234 (the experiment hall, geometry:argonne-aps-experiment-hall) has an outer way (258 vertices) that is a circle of R = 196.82 m with a 0.44 m standard deviation, and an inner way (80 vertices) whose 47 vertices lying on the circle (trimmed least squares, notches left out) give R = 169.97 m with a centre 0.6 m from the outer centre; the drawn centre is the outer-circle centre (41.7035178 N, 87.9881277 W). (3) Relation: the 1987 conceptual design report says 'The single-story experiment hall is an annular structure housing both the storage ring enclosure and the experiment floor', 'The storage ring enclosure is located inside the inner perimeter wall of the experiment hall', 'The enclosure is basically circular in plan' and 'The inside wall of the concrete tunnel is parallel to the storage ring', and that the hall is '91 ft wide ... in circumference at the storage ring centerline' (src:geo-argonne-aps-cdr-1987). The OSM annulus is 26.8 m wide (196.82 - 169.97 m) against 91 ft = 27.7 m, which says the two outlines are that hall; the orbit is therefore taken as concentric with the annulus, 5.6 m outside the radius of the inner outline and 21.2 m inside the outer outline. Cross-checks that were not used in the construction: the OSM APS linac building (411) and injection wing (412) lie 75-137 m and 44-81 m from the drawn centre, i.e. inside the infield, as the report puts 'the machine-support structures' (linac, injection and synchrotron buildings) 'in the infield of the storage ring'. What is not sourced: the beam's exact offset inside the enclosure (the report gives the enclosure interior as 11.6 ft to 18.9 ft wide, walls 0.8 m, a utility corridor of about 1.7 m) and any survey of the ring centre; hence accuracy_m 10 and confidence 'derived'. Sampled at 360 vertices (every 1 degree, chord error 0.007 m); haversine on R = 6371008.8 m measures 1103.595 m.",
  "name": "APS storage ring orbit (1103.609 m circumference, 40 sectors), derived circle",
  "notes": [
    "The Atlas has no accelerator record for the APS yet, so this feature is attached to the Argonne campus site record. The ring's start date is not recorded in the Atlas, so the feature is drawn in every year.",
    "The circumference is that of the present multi-bend-achromat lattice (1103.609 m, APS operations page, 2024); the older OSTI parameter list gives 1104 m; the 1987 design report planned 1060 m. The radius difference between the 1104 m and 1060 m rings (7 m) is why the design report cannot give the as-built position."
  ],
